# 3. WhatsApp window and template strategy

## Current technical weakness to fix

A free-form interactive merchant card is delivered only when the merchant has recently messaged the Alo King merchant number. This means a restaurant can miss a new order even though the platform successfully sent a WhatsApp API request.

The system must distinguish:

```text
API request accepted
message sent
message delivered
message read
merchant acknowledged
```

Only the last state proves operational receipt.

## Required template messages

Create and submit approved **Utility templates** for merchant order events, subject to Meta’s current template rules and pricing.

Recommended templates:

```text
merchant_new_order
merchant_order_reminder
merchant_order_escalation
merchant_order_cancelled
merchant_customer_update_required
merchant_substitution_request
merchant_driver_arriving
merchant_daily_summary
```

The new-order template should include:

```text
Alo King order {{1}} from {{2}} is waiting for confirmation.
Total: {{3}}.
Delivery area: {{4}}.
Please open the order to accept or reject it.
```

The template should link to a signed merchant portal action page. The merchant can then tap **Accept** or **Reject** in the portal even if the WhatsApp interactive button cannot be used.

Do not put a long order or full address into the template body. Keep the full order in the authenticated portal and the interactive follow-up card.

## Merchant opt-in and reactivation

During onboarding, the merchant explicitly agrees to receive transactional order notifications on the merchant WhatsApp number. The merchant should send a setup message such as:

```text
START ALO KING ORDERS
```

This establishes an active operational relationship and confirms the number. Still maintain the approved template fallback for future notifications.

At onboarding, ask the merchant to keep the number active and reply to a periodic operational check:

> Alo King merchant notifications are active. Reply **TEST** to verify this number.

Do not send unnecessary promotional content to the merchant number. Keep the channel transactional and high-trust.

