# 4. Notification routing and redundancy

## Merchant notification profile

Each merchant must configure:

```text
primary_whatsapp_members
backup_whatsapp_members
operational_phone
portal_users
notification_hours
average_prep_time
maximum_acceptance_time
order_volume_limit
holiday/closure schedule
```

At least two active merchant members should be configured before full ordering is enabled:

```text
Primary: kitchen/order operator
Backup: owner or manager
```

A single-person restaurant may use one member during soft launch but should have an Alo King operations fallback.

## Notification sequence

Recommended default timers:

```text
T+0 seconds: WhatsApp interactive card + portal alert
T+15 seconds: confirm delivery result; if not delivered, send Utility template
T+45 seconds: notify backup WhatsApp member and portal escalation
T+90 seconds: customer is told confirmation is taking longer; operations alert created
T+120 seconds: SMS to operational phone if configured
T+180 seconds: automated call or human call
T+5 minutes: stop accepting new orders from that merchant unless operations takes ownership
T+7 minutes: customer chooses keep waiting or cancel
T+10 minutes: cancel automatically only under the merchant’s agreed policy and after customer notification
```

Do not use one timer for every merchant. A high-volume restaurant with a 5-minute acceptance SLA needs a different policy from a small village bakery. Store the SLA per merchant and per zone.

## What happens if the merchant does not respond

The order remains `pending_vendor_confirmation`, but the system must stop blindly waiting.

At each escalation:

1. Re-check whether a duplicate or late acceptance already occurred.
2. Re-check merchant open/paused status.
3. Re-check whether the item became unavailable.
4. Send the next notification through the next available channel.
5. Notify the customer truthfully.
6. Create an operations task.
7. Pause new orders for that merchant if the failure threshold is reached.

Customer message:

> We’re still waiting for **[Restaurant]** to confirm order **AK-4827**. You can keep waiting or cancel without a cancellation fee.

Buttons:

```text
Keep waiting
Cancel order
Choose another
```

Never auto-accept an unacknowledged order.

