# 5. Merchant portal design

## New Order screen

The first screen should show only operationally important information:

```text
NEW ORDER #AK-4827
Deadline to accept: 01:12

Customer: [first name]
Delivery zone: [village]
Payment: COD / prepaid
Total: USD + LBP

Items
[large readable list]

Customer note
[readable note]

[ACCEPT] [REJECT] [NEED HELP]
```

The portal must provide a loud but respectful alert, a visible countdown, and an acknowledgement state.

## Accepted Order screen

```text
Order #AK-4827
Accepted at 12:41
Prep due: 13:01

[START PREPARING]
[MARK READY]
[ITEM UNAVAILABLE]
[CONTACT ALO KING]
```

## Ready screen

The merchant taps **Mark ready** only when:

- the order is packed;
- the correct items are present;
- the receipt/order code is visible;
- the handoff area is ready.

Then Alo King dispatches or confirms the driver pickup.

## Restaurant pause controls

Merchant actions:

```text
Pause for 15 minutes
Pause for 30 minutes
Pause until opening
Close now
Reduce order capacity
```

Every pause requires a reason and creates an audit event. A pause must immediately block new customer checkout while allowing active orders to continue.

