# 6. Customer, merchant, driver, and operations timeline

## Customer confirmation

```text
Order created
Customer receives receipt and waiting status
Merchant is notified
```

## Merchant accepts

```text
Customer receives acceptance and prep ETA
Merchant queue receives order
Driver dispatch is scheduled based on prep time
```

## Merchant starts preparing

No unnecessary customer message is required if the acceptance message already included a prep ETA. Record the status internally.

## Merchant marks ready

```text
Driver assignment begins or is confirmed
Merchant receives driver name/code when assigned
Customer sees “Your order is ready and a driver is being assigned” only if useful
```

## Driver picks up

```text
Merchant confirms handoff
Driver receives customer landmark and contact policy
Customer receives “On the way” plus tracking link
```

## Driver arrives

```text
Customer receives “Your driver is nearby”
Driver sees the approved delivery details
Merchant sees completed handoff
```

## Delivery complete

Use a delivery proof policy appropriate to the order:

```text
customer confirmation code, or
customer tap/confirmation, or
approved delivery photo without exposing sensitive data
```

Then:

- mark delivered;
- reconcile COD;
- send receipt and rating prompt;
- close merchant task;
- start driver settlement record.

