# 9. Security and authorization

## Every merchant action must verify

```text
WhatsApp sender or portal session
active merchant membership
vendor_id
order_id
allowed role
current order state
one-time action token / idempotency key
```

A merchant member must not be able to:

- accept another vendor’s order;
- change an old order’s price;
- view unrelated customer orders;
- access customer payment credentials;
- reveal platform margins;
- modify settlement records;
- grant themselves owner access.

## Button security

WhatsApp button IDs contain opaque references only. They must not contain:

- price;
- customer phone;
- address;
- secret;
- authorization decision.

The backend resolves the order and re-checks state. A button tap after expiry is safely rejected.

## Portal links

Use short-lived signed links with:

```text
merchant_id
order_id
action
expiry
nonce
```

A link should open a login or verified session if the action is sensitive. Do not put secrets in URL query strings.

