# 10. Notification data model

Add or formalize these tables:

```text
merchant_notification_profiles
merchant_notification_members
merchant_notification_channels
merchant_order_notifications
merchant_order_notification_attempts
merchant_order_decisions
merchant_escalations
merchant_operational_tasks
merchant_sla_events
merchant_pauses
```

Recommended notification fields:

```text
order_id
vendor_id
recipient_member_id
channel: whatsapp | portal | sms | voice | ops
message_type
provider_message_id
status: queued | sent | delivered | read | failed | acknowledged | expired
attempt_number
sent_at
delivered_at
read_at
acknowledged_at
failure_code
failure_reason
created_at
```

Recommended order fields:

```text
vendor_confirmation_deadline
vendor_first_notified_at
vendor_last_notified_at
vendor_acknowledged_at
vendor_decision_at
vendor_decision_by
vendor_rejection_reason
vendor_escalation_level
customer_waiting_choice
```

Use an outbox pattern. The order transaction creates the outbox row; a worker sends it and records the provider response. This prevents an order from existing without a notification task.

