# 12. Merchant service-level policy

Each merchant signs or accepts a simple operating policy:

```text
Accept or reject within: [default 90 seconds]
Start preparation within: [configured time]
Mark ready by: accepted time + prep time
Keep menu availability current
Pause orders when overloaded
Respond to substitution requests
Keep at least one operational member active
Maintain a backup contact
```

## Suggested performance thresholds

Use a rolling seven-day window:

| Metric | Healthy | Warning | Pause/review |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Acceptance within SLA | ≥95% | 85–94% | <85% |
| Rejection after acceptance | <3% | 3–7% | >7% |
| Merchant timeout rate | <2% | 2–5% | >5% |
| Ready-on-time rate | ≥90% | 80–89% | <80% |
| Customer complaint rate | <3% | 3–6% | >6% |
| Menu-induced cancellation | <2% | 2–5% | >5% |

These are starting operating thresholds, not permanent marketplace rules. Adjust them after pilot data.

## Consequences

```text
Warning → merchant coaching and menu review
Restricted → lower order volume or longer prep ETA
Paused → no new orders until merchant confirms readiness
Suspended → manual review and re-verification
```

Do not punish a merchant for a single telecom outage or force acceptance during a documented emergency.

