## P0 — fix before accepting real orders

1. Replace “message sent” with explicit sent/delivered/read/acknowledged states.
2. Build the merchant notification outbox.
3. Add Utility template fallback for new orders.
4. Add the portal new-order queue with sound and countdown.
5. Add backup recipient routing.
6. Add typed accept/reject/need-help actions.
7. Add the 90-second customer/operations escalation.
8. Add merchant pause and capacity controls.
9. Add notification attempt audit logs.
10. Add duplicate-tap and duplicate-webhook protection.

## P1 — complete the operational system

1. Add SMS and phone escalation.
2. Add substitution and item-unavailable workflows.
3. Add merchant SLA dashboards.
4. Add role-based merchant members.
5. Add driver-readiness integration.
6. Add notification failure monitoring.
7. Add merchant daily summaries.
8. Add order printer/KDS integration only after portal reliability is proven.

## P2 — optimize

1. Predict merchant acceptance time.
2. Select the best notification channel by historical reliability.
3. Adjust acceptance windows by merchant type and zone.
4. Forecast kitchen capacity.
5. Automatically pause a merchant before failure when capacity risk is high.
6. Measure the cost and conversion impact of WhatsApp, portal, SMS, and voice channels.

