# Final decision

> **Alo King should accept a vendor order only after the merchant has a reliable notification path, a visible portal queue, a backup contact, and an explicit acceptance event.**

The perfect practical setup is:

```text
Customer confirms
→ order is created as pending vendor confirmation
→ WhatsApp interactive card is sent
→ delivery is verified
→ approved Utility template is used when needed
→ portal alert remains active
→ backup WhatsApp/SMS/voice escalation starts on timeout
→ merchant explicitly accepts or rejects
→ customer is updated
→ preparation and driver dispatch begin
→ every event is auditable
```

WhatsApp should be the **fastest and most natural merchant channel**. The portal should be the **operational source of truth**. SMS and voice should be the **recovery layer**. Alo King operations should be the **final safety net**.
